# name: test/sql/f5_payer_alive.test
# description: F5 payer-alive (BG/NBD), exercised as the collections agent would use it
# group: [sql]

require anofox_bayes

#######################################
# Setup: a customer base, one row per payer
#######################################

# 600 accounts of a subscription business, each collapsed to the three statistics the
# model reads:
#
#   frequency  repeat payments after the first one
#   recency    when the last of those arrived, in weeks from the first
#   age        how long the account has been observed, in weeks from the first
#
# The base was drawn from the model itself (r = 1.2, alpha = 10, a = 1.5, b = 2.0 over
# a 78-week horizon, with accounts acquired at different times so the observation
# windows differ) and rounded to four decimals, which is why the rows are literal
# rather than generated: the same table then feeds the Rust unit tests and this file,
# and the two cannot drift.
#
# It contains what a real book contains -- accounts that never repeated, accounts
# still paying up to the edge of their window, and accounts that paid for a while and
# then went silent. Nothing marks which is which. Working that out is the model's job.
statement ok
CREATE TABLE payers(customer_id INTEGER, frequency INTEGER, recency DOUBLE, age DOUBLE);

statement ok
